# Intentionally empty. Nextup OSS environments use per-environment templates:
#   env/dev.env.example      -> .env.dev      (created by scripts/local.py --env dev start)
#   env/staging.env.example  -> .env.staging  (created manually, mode 0600)
# scripts/verify_ci.py passes this file to its disposable CI stack only so that no
# developer .env is ever read there; compose.ci.yaml needs no values from it.
